<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Saud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1875">1875</a>–<a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud, Abdulaziz ibn Abdul Rahman Al Saud, Abdulaziz ibn Saud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Saud, Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a> ibn Abd al-Rahman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a>, recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> from the Rashidis in 1902 and rebuilt Saudi power in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Hasa</a> in 1913, destroyed the Rashidi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of Jabal Shammar in 1921 and conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> in 1924–1925. In 1932 he united his lands as the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, where oil was found in 1938.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-saud.jpg" alt="Ibn Saud" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saudi Press Agency · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Official_Portrait_of_King_Abdulaziz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
